Complements fix-before-request-params-not-cleared.patch: makes the fix
self-healing for customer sessions that were already poisoned before that
patch was deployed.

Context: before_request_params is stored in the customer session so
Wishlist\Controller\Index\Add::execute() can replay the original request
of a guest who got redirected to login while adding a product to the
wishlist (see the already-applied fix-adding-to-wishlist.patch). It used to
never be cleared, so once set it silently overrode the real POST data of
every subsequent add-to-wishlist click for the rest of that session -
always re-processing the same, stale product. fix-before-request-
params-not-cleared.patch stops it from being set permanently going
forward, but a session that was poisoned before that fix was deployed
never dispatches the code path that clears it again (before_wishlist_request
is already gone), so it stays stuck until the session ends.

Fix: clear before_request_params in Add::execute() itself, right after it
is read. This makes it single-use at the point of consumption regardless of
which code path set it, so an already-poisoned session heals itself after
one more add-to-wishlist request instead of staying broken indefinitely.

